# Intent: Bench only (CONFIG_MAIPAI_SERIAL_TOOLS, and CONFIG_MAIPAI_TALK_OVER for the tone check). self.bench.set_head {yaw, pitch, speed, hold_ms} moves the head whatever the idle movement setting is, through the servo layer so the movement limiter still applies, and answers the angles read back from the servo bus. self.bench.mic3_check now sets the speaker volume it is given (0 is the silent speaker case, the saved volume comes back), listens for one second of room and 2.5 s of tone, and answers medians over 200 ms windows for both input channels.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: on a talkover bench image self.bench.set_head yaw 40 pitch 10 answers read-back angles near 40 and 10; mic3_check at volume 0 and at 70 answers different ch1 tone medians when the second channel is the speaker loopback.
# Kconfig: CONFIG_MAIPAI_SERIAL_TOOLS, CONFIG_MAIPAI_TALK_OVER (existing)

